WEBVTT

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:04.320
An Illinois business owner
told Federal Reserve researchers,

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:07.885
“I hope to see rates, terms
and what I qualified for.”

00:00:07.948 --> 00:00:10.550
When repayment comes from daily sales,

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:13.680
what will be left for payroll
on a slow week?

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:16.820
Barbara Lipman and Ann Marie Wiersch

00:00:16.945 --> 00:00:20.535
asked 42 owners to compare sample offers.

00:00:20.565 --> 00:00:22.812
Many struggled to understand the costs.

00:00:22.812 --> 00:00:26.858
When the researchers reviewed
10 online lenders’ websites,

00:00:26.858 --> 00:00:30.136
some cash advance providers
gave no price at all.

00:00:30.356 --> 00:00:35.619
EXL asked how lenders could design
better offers for shoppers at checkout.

00:00:35.619 --> 00:00:37.909
Its researchers recommended testing

00:00:37.909 --> 00:00:41.701
amount, rate and term
across different customers.

00:00:41.701 --> 00:00:45.292
I borrowed that method
to explore offers for the merchant.

00:00:45.731 --> 00:00:51.800
Russel, Shi and Clarke studied why
payment processors can finance merchants.

00:00:51.956 --> 00:00:53.376
Eight months after funding,

00:00:53.376 --> 00:00:58.633
recipients processed 16% less
through one South African provider

00:00:58.653 --> 00:01:00.568
than similar firms that passed.

00:01:00.568 --> 00:01:04.859
Who sought financing and where merchants
routed sales both mattered.

00:01:05.089 --> 00:01:09.479
Those studies inspired me to follow
an offer through to repayment.

00:01:09.479 --> 00:01:12.994
In one simulation, the same merchant
took identical terms.

00:01:12.994 --> 00:01:15.097
It paid in full under Baseline.

00:01:15.097 --> 00:01:20.767
Under energy stress, it still owed
about $3,700 on day 120.

00:01:20.997 --> 00:01:24.506
The Fed has no dedicated
merchant cash advance rule.

00:01:24.506 --> 00:01:26.776
For state member banks making loans,

00:01:26.776 --> 00:01:30.406
its standards call for documenting
the repayment source

00:01:30.429 --> 00:01:33.042
and assessing whether
the borrower can pay.

00:01:33.199 --> 00:01:35.589
The Consumer Financial Protection Bureau

00:01:35.589 --> 00:01:41.889
excludes qualifying merchant cash advances
from Section 1071 reporting.

00:01:42.095 --> 00:01:46.042
Other fair-lending duties depend on
whether the agreement is credit.

00:01:46.245 --> 00:01:51.851
The Reserve Banks expect new
small-business survey results in 2027.

00:01:51.894 --> 00:01:55.602
My next test is whether the offers
that work in simulation

00:01:55.602 --> 00:01:59.820
also leave real merchants
enough cash to operate and repay.

